# Vendored third-party files must stay BYTE-IDENTICAL to what upstream published.
#
# Without this, git's autocrlf normalises leaflet.js/.css to CRLF in a Windows working tree.
# The committed blob would still be LF, but the file on disk would no longer match the sha256
# that scripts/vendor-leaflet.mjs prints and that the L1 commit records — so a genuine
# integrity check would look like a mismatch, and a real mismatch could hide in the noise.
# `-text` disables all end-of-line conversion for this tree.
public/vendor/** -text

# Same reasoning for the generated icon set: these are binary, and any conversion corrupts them.
# (Git detects most binaries automatically; this makes it explicit for the .ico and .svg, the
# latter being text-like enough that autocrlf would otherwise touch it.)
public/favicon.ico -text
public/favicon.svg -text
